# Offline oracle note — dos-spin-si (PW collinear-spin DOS, diamond Si)

## Purpose

Character / wall twin for `regressions/pw/dos-spin-si`. **Not** an absolute
DOS pin: CP2K Quickstep uses GTH-PADE + DZVP-GTH; Atomiverse PW uses ONCV
UPF. Record CP2K version, wall, and occupied-state integral character when
a binary is available. Never launch CP2K from ctest.

## Suggested CP2K settings (LSD + denser k for DOS character)

```
&GLOBAL
  PROJECT si_dos_spin_wall
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
  PRINT_LEVEL MEDIUM
&END GLOBAL
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    LSD
    MULTIPLICITY 1
    &QS
      EPS_DEFAULT 1.0E-10
    &END QS
    &MGRID
      CUTOFF 300
      REL_CUTOFF 60
    &END MGRID
    &SCF
      SCF_GUESS ATOMIC
      EPS_SCF 1.0E-6
      MAX_SCF 50
      &DIAGONALIZATION
        ALGORITHM STANDARD
      &END DIAGONALIZATION
      &MIXING
        METHOD BROYDEN_MIXING
        ALPHA 0.4
      &END MIXING
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PADE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
    &KPOINTS
      SCHEME MONKHORST-PACK 2 2 2
    &END KPOINTS
    &PRINT
      &PDOS
        NLUMO 4
        COMPONENTS .FALSE.
      &END PDOS
    &END PRINT
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      A 0.0 2.715 2.715
      B 2.715 0.0 2.715
      C 2.715 2.715 0.0
      PERIODIC XYZ
    &END CELL
    &COORD
      Si 0.0 0.0 0.0
      Si 1.3575 1.3575 1.3575
    &END COORD
    &KIND Si
      BASIS_SET DZVP-GTH-q4
      POTENTIAL GTH-PADE-q4
    &END KIND
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
```

## Pins written to REFERENCE.md

See `regressions/pw/dos-spin-si/REFERENCE.md`. Scientific pins: SCF
converges with \(M=0\); \(\int^{E_\mathrm{vbm}} D(E)\,dE \approx 8\);
open gap on the denser DOS mesh. Absolute \(D(E)\) not comparable across
ONCV-PW vs GTH-GPW.
